{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1781410938033,"sessionID":"ses_13ba27f37ffe7zM3c3M9tb1iZ0","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_VcIc2ENFfwXmCplAiG62SChH","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/stale_policy_excerpt.md","offset":1,"limit":400},"output":"<path>/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/stale_policy_excerpt.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Stale Policy Excerpt\n2: \n3: Policy date: 2026-03-01\n4: \n5: This excerpt was copied into the travel folder before the finance policy update.\n6: \n7: Older rules:\n8: \n9: - Receipts are required only for expenses over $100.00.\n10: - Lodging is reimbursable up to $260.00 per night.\n11: - Ride-share tips are reimbursable up to 25% of the base fare.\n12: - Seat upgrades are reimbursable up to $50.00 when booked with economy airfare.\n13: \n14: Important: this excerpt may be stale if a newer policy applies.\n\n(End of file - total 14 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Stale Policy Excerpt\n\nPolicy date: 2026-03-01\n\nThis excerpt was copied into the travel folder before the finance policy update.\n\nOlder rules:\n\n- Receipts are required only for expenses over $100.00.\n- Lodging is reimbursable up to $260.00 per night.\n- Ride-share tips are reimbursable up to 25% of the base fare.\n- Seat upgrades are reimbursable up to $50.00 when booked with economy airfare.\n\nImportant: this excerpt may be stale if a newer policy applies.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/stale_policy_excerpt.md","text":"# Stale Policy Excerpt\n\nPolicy date: 2026-03-01\n\nThis excerpt was copied into the travel folder before the finance policy update.\n\nOlder rules:\n\n- Receipts are required only for expenses over $100.00.\n- Lodging is reimbursable up to $260.00 per night.\n- Ride-share tips are reimbursable up to 25% of the base fare.\n- Seat upgrades are reimbursable up to $50.00 when booked with economy airfare.\n\nImportant: this excerpt may be stale if a newer policy applies.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":14,"totalLines":14,"truncated":false}},"title":"tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/stale_policy_excerpt.md","time":{"start":1781410938010,"end":1781410938029}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_04658e56ad3d4c74016a2e2c79dcd8819189ef400022a1c454"}},"id":"prt_ec45dbc96001KXbXvaXEIUgpcg","sessionID":"ses_13ba27f37ffe7zM3c3M9tb1iZ0","messageID":"msg_ec45da75f001cwmdljG6VmZu8H"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1781410938033,"sessionID":"ses_13ba27f37ffe7zM3c3M9tb1iZ0","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_eF5eh5lT3xDvJUgJu6sLJNHs","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/receipts.md","offset":1,"limit":400},"output":"<path>/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/receipts.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Receipt Evidence\n2: \n3: - T-001: Receipt present. Economy round-trip airfare, $480.00.\n4: - T-002: Receipt present. Exit-row seat upgrade, $45.00. No written preapproval is included.\n5: - T-003: Receipt present. Hotel folio total $510.00 for two nights, including room, taxes, and mandatory fees.\n6: - T-004: Receipt present. Food subtotal $58.00 and wine $18.00, total $76.00.\n7: - T-005: Receipt present. Base fare $50.00 and tip $20.00, total $70.00.\n8: - T-006: No receipt provided. Business purpose note says \"USB-C adapters for demo room.\"\n9: - T-007: Receipt present. Breakfast, $18.00.\n\n(End of file - total 9 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Receipt Evidence\n\n- T-001: Receipt present. Economy round-trip airfare, $480.00.\n- T-002: Receipt present. Exit-row seat upgrade, $45.00. No written preapproval is included.\n- T-003: Receipt present. Hotel folio total $510.00 for two nights, including room, taxes, and mandatory fees.\n- T-004: Receipt present. Food subtotal $58.00 and wine $18.00, total $76.00.\n- T-005: Receipt present. Base fare $50.00 and tip $20.00, total $70.00.\n- T-006: No receipt provided. Business purpose note says \"USB-C adapters for demo room.\"\n- T-007: Receipt present. Breakfast, $18.00.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/receipts.md","text":"# Receipt Evidence\n\n- T-001: Receipt present. Economy round-trip airfare, $480.00.\n- T-002: Receipt present. Exit-row seat upgrade, $45.00. No written preapproval is included.\n- T-003: Receipt present. Hotel folio total $510.00 for two nights, including room, taxes, and mandatory fees.\n- T-004: Receipt present. Food subtotal $58.00 and wine $18.00, total $76.00.\n- T-005: Receipt present. Base fare $50.00 and tip $20.00, total $70.00.\n- T-006: No receipt provided. Business purpose note says \"USB-C adapters for demo room.\"\n- T-007: Receipt present. Breakfast, $18.00.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":9,"totalLines":9,"truncated":false}},"title":"tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/receipts.md","time":{"start":1781410938015,"end":1781410938031}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_04658e56ad3d4c74016a2e2c79dcdc8191ba83cf02a0eca153"}},"id":"prt_ec45dbc9c001vKH0tOMWgaUlS2","sessionID":"ses_13ba27f37ffe7zM3c3M9tb1iZ0","messageID":"msg_ec45da75f001cwmdljG6VmZu8H"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1781410938042,"sessionID":"ses_13ba27f37ffe7zM3c3M9tb1iZ0","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_b4n2VfTfstL5lMd3iCpDOu2b","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/current_policy.md","offset":1,"limit":400},"output":"<path>/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/current_policy.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Current Finance Travel Policy\n2: \n3: Policy date: 2026-04-20\n4: \n5: Effective for trips starting on or after 2026-05-01. This policy supersedes older travel policy excerpts for covered trips.\n6: \n7: General rules:\n8: \n9: - Use this current policy when it conflicts with older policy excerpts.\n10: - Receipts are required for every expense of $75.00 or more.\n11: - Expenses without required receipts are not reimbursable when a receipt is required.\n12: \n13: Air travel:\n14: \n15: - Economy airfare is reimbursable with a receipt.\n16: - Seat upgrades, extra-legroom fees, priority boarding, and similar optional upgrades are not reimbursable unless written preapproval is provided in the receipt evidence. No preapproval means no reimbursement.\n17: \n18: Lodging:\n19: \n20: - Lodging is reimbursable up to $220.00 per night, including room, taxes, and mandatory fees.\n21: - Apply the cap by multiplying covered nights by $220.00.\n22: \n23: Meals:\n24: \n25: - Meals are reimbursable at actual cost up to $65.00 per day.\n26: - Alcohol is not reimbursable and must be removed from meal receipts.\n27: \n28: Ride-share:\n29: \n30: - Ride-share base fare is reimbursable with a receipt.\n31: - Tips are reimbursable up to 20% of the base fare.\n32: - Any tip amount above 20% of the base fare is not reimbursable.\n33: \n34: Supplies:\n35: \n36: - Work supplies can be reimbursed only when a required receipt is provided and the business purpose is clear.\n37: \n38: Trip covered by this audit:\n39: \n40: - Employee: Jordan Lee\n41: - Trip dates: 2026-05-08 to 2026-05-10\n42: - Covered lodging nights: 2\n\n(End of file - total 42 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Current Finance Travel Policy\n\nPolicy date: 2026-04-20\n\nEffective for trips starting on or after 2026-05-01. This policy supersedes older travel policy excerpts for covered trips.\n\nGeneral rules:\n\n- Use this current policy when it conflicts with older policy excerpts.\n- Receipts are required for every expense of $75.00 or more.\n- Expenses without required receipts are not reimbursable when a receipt is required.\n\nAir travel:\n\n- Economy airfare is reimbursable with a receipt.\n- Seat upgrades, extra-legroom fees, priority boarding, and similar optional upgrades are not reimbursable unless written preapproval is provided in the receipt evidence. No preapproval means no reimbursement.\n\nLodging:\n\n- Lodging is reimbursable up to $220.00 per night, including room, taxes, and mandatory fees.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/current_policy.md","text":"# Current Finance Travel Policy\n\nPolicy date: 2026-04-20\n\nEffective for trips starting on or after 2026-05-01. This policy supersedes older travel policy excerpts for covered trips.\n\nGeneral rules:\n\n- Use this current policy when it conflicts with older policy excerpts.\n- Receipts are required for every expense of $75.00 or more.\n- Expenses without required receipts are not reimbursable when a receipt is required.\n\nAir travel:\n\n- Economy airfare is reimbursable with a receipt.\n- Seat upgrades, extra-legroom fees, priority boarding, and similar optional upgrades are not reimbursable unless written preapproval is provided in the receipt evidence. No preapproval means no reimbursement.\n\nLodging:\n\n- Lodging is reimbursable up to $220.00 per night, including room, taxes, and mandatory fees.\n- Apply the cap by multiplying covered nights by $220.00.\n\nMeals:\n\n- Meals are reimbursable at actual cost up to $65.00 per day.\n- Alcohol is not reimbursable and must be removed from meal receipts.\n\nRide-share:\n\n- Ride-share base fare is reimbursable with a receipt.\n- Tips are reimbursable up to 20% of the base fare.\n- Any tip amount above 20% of the base fare is not reimbursable.\n\nSupplies:\n\n- Work supplies can be reimbursed only when a required receipt is provided and the business purpose is clear.\n\nTrip covered by this audit:\n\n- Employee: Jordan Lee\n- Trip dates: 2026-05-08 to 2026-05-10\n- Covered lodging nights: 2","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":42,"totalLines":42,"truncated":false}},"title":"tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/current_policy.md","time":{"start":1781410938004,"end":1781410938034}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_04658e56ad3d4c74016a2e2c79dcd0819199c9f7e1253eef51"}},"id":"prt_ec45dbc90001auUFx8fqV24p9f","sessionID":"ses_13ba27f37ffe7zM3c3M9tb1iZ0","messageID":"msg_ec45da75f001cwmdljG6VmZu8H"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1781410938042,"sessionID":"ses_13ba27f37ffe7zM3c3M9tb1iZ0","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_PaoQ3Oebc7v8Ode0z8zr26eo","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/output_contract.md","offset":1,"limit":400},"output":"<path>/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/output_contract.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Deliverable Contract\n2: \n3: Create an `answer/` folder in this task folder, then create these three files inside it. The format may be Markdown tables or concise labeled sections, but the paths, filenames, and required facts must be present.\n4: \n5: ## `answer/policy_application.md`\n6: \n7: Record which policy source controls this audit and the rules applied.\n8: \n9: Required facts:\n10: \n11: - The trip dates being audited.\n12: - The current policy date and why it supersedes the stale policy excerpt.\n13: - The receipt threshold.\n14: - The seat-upgrade rule.\n15: - The lodging cap calculation basis.\n16: - The meal and alcohol rule.\n17: - The ride-share tip cap.\n18: - The supplies receipt rule.\n19: \n20: ## `answer/expense_decisions.md`\n21: \n22: Record the item-level audit decision for every expense.\n23: \n24: Required facts:\n25: \n26: - One row or entry for every expense ID in `expenses.csv`.\n27: - For each expense: claimed amount, approved amount, non-reimbursable amount, status (`approved`, `partial`, or `rejected`), and the policy or receipt reason.\n28: \n29: ## `answer/reimbursement_summary.md`\n30: \n31: Write the final reimbursement summary for the finance teammate.\n32: \n33: Required facts:\n34: \n35: - Reimbursable total.\n36: - Non-reimbursable total.\n37: - Arithmetic showing how the reimbursable total was calculated.\n38: - Fully approved expense IDs.\n39: - Partially reimbursed or capped expense IDs.\n40: - Rejected expense IDs.\n41: \n42: Rules:\n43: \n44: - Use local files only.\n45: - Do not put the required deliverables in the task root; put them under `answer/`.\n46: - Use dollar amounts rounded to two decimal places when needed.\n47: - Extra scratch files are allowed, but scoring is based on the three named deliverables under `answer/`.\n\n(End of file - total 47 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Deliverable Contract\n\nCreate an `answer/` folder in this task folder, then create these three files inside it. The format may be Markdown tables or concise labeled sections, but the paths, filenames, and required facts must be present.\n\n## `answer/policy_application.md`\n\nRecord which policy source controls this audit and the rules applied.\n\nRequired facts:\n\n- The trip dates being audited.\n- The current policy date and why it supersedes the stale policy excerpt.\n- The receipt threshold.\n- The seat-upgrade rule.\n- The lodging cap calculation basis.\n- The meal and alcohol rule.\n- The ride-share tip cap.\n- The supplies receipt rule.\n\n## `answer/expense_decisions.md`","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/output_contract.md","text":"# Deliverable Contract\n\nCreate an `answer/` folder in this task folder, then create these three files inside it. The format may be Markdown tables or concise labeled sections, but the paths, filenames, and required facts must be present.\n\n## `answer/policy_application.md`\n\nRecord which policy source controls this audit and the rules applied.\n\nRequired facts:\n\n- The trip dates being audited.\n- The current policy date and why it supersedes the stale policy excerpt.\n- The receipt threshold.\n- The seat-upgrade rule.\n- The lodging cap calculation basis.\n- The meal and alcohol rule.\n- The ride-share tip cap.\n- The supplies receipt rule.\n\n## `answer/expense_decisions.md`\n\nRecord the item-level audit decision for every expense.\n\nRequired facts:\n\n- One row or entry for every expense ID in `expenses.csv`.\n- For each expense: claimed amount, approved amount, non-reimbursable amount, status (`approved`, `partial`, or `rejected`), and the policy or receipt reason.\n\n## `answer/reimbursement_summary.md`\n\nWrite the final reimbursement summary for the finance teammate.\n\nRequired facts:\n\n- Reimbursable total.\n- Non-reimbursable total.\n- Arithmetic showing how the reimbursable total was calculated.\n- Fully approved expense IDs.\n- Partially reimbursed or capped expense IDs.\n- Rejected expense IDs.\n\nRules:\n\n- Use local files only.\n- Do not put the required deliverables in the task root; put them under `answer/`.\n- Use dollar amounts rounded to two decimal places when needed.\n- Extra scratch files are allowed, but scoring is based on the three named deliverables under `answer/`.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":47,"totalLines":47,"truncated":false}},"title":"tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/output_contract.md","time":{"start":1781410937994,"end":1781410938035}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_04658e56ad3d4c74016a2e2c79dcc08191a851be21c3859084"}},"id":"prt_ec45dbc80001jsMds0cbJZ87ac","sessionID":"ses_13ba27f37ffe7zM3c3M9tb1iZ0","messageID":"msg_ec45da75f001cwmdljG6VmZu8H"}}
