{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1781410966714,"sessionID":"ses_13ba27f37ffe7zM3c3M9tb1iZ0","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_KIwm5SFQovklSUFq0YuUuoFk","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/policy_application.md\n+## Policy Selection Checkpoint\n+\n+- Trip dates audited: `2026-05-08` to `2026-05-10`.\n+- Controlling policy source: `current_policy.md`.\n+- Current policy date: `2026-04-20`.\n+- Why it supersedes the stale excerpt: the current policy is effective for trips starting on or after `2026-05-01`, this trip started on `2026-05-08`, and the current policy explicitly states that it supersedes older travel policy excerpts for covered trips.\n+\n+## Rules Applied Checkpoint\n+\n+- Receipt threshold: receipts are required for every expense of `$75.00` or more.\n+- Seat-upgrade rule: seat upgrades, extra-legroom fees, priority boarding, and similar optional upgrades are not reimbursable unless written preapproval is included in the receipt evidence.\n+- Lodging cap calculation basis: lodging is capped at `$220.00` per covered night, including room, taxes, and mandatory fees; with `2` covered nights, the maximum reimbursable lodging amount is `2 x $220.00 = $440.00`.\n+- Meal and alcohol rule: meals are reimbursable at actual cost up to `$65.00` per day, and alcohol must be removed from meal receipts as non-reimbursable.\n+- Ride-share tip cap: ride-share base fare is reimbursable with a receipt, and tips are reimbursable only up to `20%` of the base fare.\n+- Supplies receipt rule: work supplies are reimbursable only when a required receipt is provided and the business purpose is clear.\n*** Add File: /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/expense_decisions.md\n+## Item-Level Audit Checkpoint\n+\n+| Expense ID | Claimed Amount | Approved Amount | Non-Reimbursable Amount | Status | Reason |\n+| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- | --- |\n+| T-001 | $480.00 | $480.00 | $0.00 | approved | Economy airfare with receipt is reimbursable under the current air-travel policy. |\n+| T-002 | $45.00 | $0.00 | $45.00 | rejected | Optional seat upgrade is not reimbursable without written preapproval; receipt evidence shows no preapproval. |\n+| T-003 | $510.00 | $440.00 | $70.00 | partial | Lodging is capped at $220.00 per covered night; `2 x $220.00 = $440.00`, so the excess above the cap is not reimbursable. |\n+| T-004 | $76.00 | $58.00 | $18.00 | partial | Meal receipt includes $18.00 of wine; alcohol must be removed from meal reimbursement. The remaining food subtotal is within the daily meal cap. |\n+| T-005 | $70.00 | $60.00 | $10.00 | partial | Ride-share receipt shows $50.00 base fare and $20.00 tip; only a tip up to 20% of base fare is reimbursable, so the max allowed tip is $10.00. |\n+| T-006 | $82.00 | $0.00 | $82.00 | rejected | Supplies over the $75.00 receipt threshold require a receipt. No receipt was provided, so the expense is not reimbursable even though the business purpose is stated. |\n+| T-007 | $18.00 | $18.00 | $0.00 | approved | Breakfast is a meal under the daily cap, and no receipt is required because the amount is below $75.00. |\n*** Add File: /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/reimbursement_summary.md\n+## Reimbursement Summary Checkpoint\n+\n+- Reimbursable total: `$1,056.00`\n+- Non-reimbursable total: `$225.00`\n+\n+## Calculation\n+\n+- Reimbursable total = `T-001 $480.00 + T-002 $0.00 + T-003 $440.00 + T-004 $58.00 + T-005 $60.00 + T-006 $0.00 + T-007 $18.00 = $1,056.00`\n+- Non-reimbursable total = `T-001 $0.00 + T-002 $45.00 + T-003 $70.00 + T-004 $18.00 + T-005 $10.00 + T-006 $82.00 + T-007 $0.00 = $225.00`\n+\n+## Decision Buckets\n+\n+- Fully approved expense IDs: `T-001`, `T-007`\n+- Partially reimbursed or capped expense IDs: `T-003`, `T-004`, `T-005`\n+- Rejected expense IDs: `T-002`, `T-006`\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/policy_application.md\nA tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/expense_decisions.md\nA tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/reimbursement_summary.md","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/policy_application.md\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/policy_application.md\n+++ /Users/douglas/code/masters/sbench/tasks/travel_reimbursement_audit/answer/policy_application.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@\n+## Policy Selection Checkpoint\n+\n+- Trip dates audited: `2026-05-08` to `2026-05-10`.\n+- Controlling policy source: `current_policy.md`.\n+- Current policy date: `2026-04-20`.\n+- Why it supersedes the stale excerpt: the current policy is effective for trips starting on or after `2026-05-01`, this trip started on `2026-05-08`, and the current policy explicitly states that it supersedes older travel policy excerpts for covered trips.\n+\n+## Rules Applied Checkpoint\n+\n+- Receipt threshold: receipts are required for every expense of `$75.00` or more.\n+- Seat-upgrade rule: seat upgrades, extra-legroom fees, priority boarding, and similar optional upgrades are not reimbursable unless written preapproval is included in the receipt evidence.\n+- Lodging cap calculation basis: lodging is capped at `$220.00` per covered night, including room, taxes, and mandatory fees; with `2` covered nights, the maximum reimbursable lodging amount is `2 x $220.00 = $440.00`.\n+- Meal and alcohol rule: meals are reimbursable at actual cost up to `$65.00` per day, and alcohol must be removed from meal receipts as non-reimbursable.\n+- Ride-share tip cap: ride-share base fare is reimbursable with a receipt, and tips are reimbursable only up to `20%` of the base fare.\n+- Supplies receipt rule: work supplies are